    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d181">

                <pb facs="0324" n="298" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v16/pg298"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">396.1 GE/5–1554: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Embassy in the Republic of China</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d181-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >secret<lb/>priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-05-20T17:34:00-04:00">May 20, 1954—5:34
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>888. For Secretary Wilson from the
                    Secretary. Re Tokyo’s 2808 repeated Geneva Tosec 170, Seoul 925.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d181-f2"/> Appreciate
                    your valuable suggestion. Have transmitted it Geneva for information US
                    delegation there.</p>
                <p>So far as Korea is concerned our present problem is to secure some statement
                    basic principles upon which ROK, US and rest of
                    allied delegations can all agree. There seems little likelihood achieving any
                    political settlement disturbing present <hi rendition="#italic">status quo</hi>
                    on any basis which would be acceptable to us and prevent communist domination
                    all Korea. Nevertheless it may be useful at some point incorporate provision of
                    nature your suggestion in order demonstrate more clearly to world opinion our
                    effort achieve settlement.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Dulles</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d181-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d181-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated for information to Geneva as telegram Tosec 220, to Seoul as telegram 935, and to Tokyo as telegram 2576.
                    The file copy indicates that this message was drafted by McClurkin and approved for transmission by
                        Drumright who signed for Dulles.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d181-f2" n="2" xml:id="d181-f2-content">
                <p>Dated May 15, not printed. In it, Secretary Wilson suggested inclusion in any proposal for unification of
                    Korea of a provision for personal amnesty for all individuals; he indicated that
                    Ambassador Allison agreed with him. (396.1 GE/5–1554)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
